/-!
# Pub 1 strong closure: exact sup bounds on the residual

The coefficient absolute-sum bounds of `admissible_closure.py`, in the kernel.
On `|x| ≤ 1/2` a polynomial is bounded by the sum of `|c_d| 2^(-d)`, which is
what turns the exact residual `r₀` of `Certificate.lean` into the two numbers the
certificate consumes:

* `‖r₀‖_∞ < 2.1710808e-5`
* `‖r₀''‖_∞ < 0.005982627`

`r0Coeff`, `r0Coeff1`, `r0Coeff2` are the coefficient tables of `r₀`, `r₀'` and
`r₀''`.  `r0Poly_eq_sum` reconciles the table with the closed form used by
`r0_identity`, so the two developments are about the same polynomial.
-/

open Finset

